# Frontend HTTP (`services/` & `api/`)

**Language:** Write all service/API code, comments, and related commit messages in **English**.

Applies to `ui/src/services/` and `ui/src/api/`. For Colada consumption see `pinia-colada.mdc`; for components see `vue.mdc`.

## Official documentation

- Axios is used via `ui/src/services/api/api.service.ts` — follow existing project patterns, not ad-hoc `fetch`.

## When to use which layer

| Layer                 | Path                                  | When to use                                                |
| --------------------- | ------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Class service**     | `ui/src/services/{domain}.service.ts` | Default — mutations, searches, domain flows, legacy stores |
| **Colada API helper** | `ui/src/api/{domain}.api.ts`          | Thin HTTP called only from `ui/src/queries/`               |
| **Axios client**      | `ui/src/services/api/api.service.ts`  | Low-level client — do not import in components             |

**Do not** call HTTP from `components/`, `views/`, or `stores/` directly — go through `services/` or Colada (`api/` + `queries/`).

## Path enums (required)

- Base paths: **`ApiBaseUrl`** in `ui/src/enums/api.enum.ts`
- Endpoint paths: **`UiApiUrlPathEnum`**
- HTTP methods: **`RequestMethodEnum`**

Do not hardcode `/uiapi/...` strings or full URLs in services, api helpers, or components.

## Class services (dominant pattern)

```ts
import { ApiBaseUrl, RequestMethodEnum, UiApiUrlPathEnum } from '@/enums';
import { ServiceHelper } from '@/utils/helpers';

export class CustomerService {
  static async search(params: FilterParams) {
    return ServiceHelper.requestWrapper({
      requestData: {
        method: RequestMethodEnum.POST,
        url: UiApiUrlPathEnum.CUSTOMER_SEARCH,
        data: params,
      },
    });
  }
}
```

- Export **`XxxService`** class with **static** methods (match neighbouring domain services)
- Use **`ServiceHelper.requestWrapper`** for loader, toast/popup success/error handling
- Request/response types from **`@/interfaces/`**
- Barrel: re-export from `ui/src/services/index.ts` when other domains already do

## Colada API helpers

```ts
import { UiApiUrlPathEnum } from '@/enums';
import ApiService from '../services/api/api.service';

const http = new ApiService().getClient();

export const getMyItems = async (payload: Payload) => {
  const result = await http.post(UiApiUrlPathEnum.MY_ITEMS, payload);
  return result.data;
};
```

- One function per endpoint; return **unwrapped** `result.data`
- Used by `ui/src/queries/` — not by components or stores directly
- Do not duplicate the same endpoint in both `services/` and `api/` unless migrating — prefer one layer per call site

## ServiceHelper behaviour

`ServiceHelper.requestWrapper` (in `ui/src/utils/helpers/service.helper.ts`):

- Shows/hides global loader via `loader.store` (unless `hideLoader: true`)
- Optional success/error toast or SweetAlert via `success` / `error` config
- Returns `response.data` on 2xx

Match neighbouring service calls for `hideError`, `hideLoader`, and toast/popup options.

## Before finishing

- [ ] No raw Axios/`fetch` in components, views, or stores
- [ ] URLs use `UiApiUrlPathEnum` / `ApiBaseUrl` — no magic strings
- [ ] New Colada reads: HTTP in `api/`, queries in `queries/` — not new service+store cache
- [ ] Types from `@/interfaces/` — avoid `any` on payloads
- [ ] New service methods match static class pattern in the same domain file
